WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.340
Welcome to Supplier Agreement Management. In this lesson, we explore this purpose: Select, contract with and actively manage external suppliers.

2
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:21.620
Consider this scenario. A subcontractor repeatedly supplies components outside specification. First understand the problem before producing documentation.

3
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:31.570
Start with two steps: Define supplier requirements. Then Assess and select candidates. Each step should be explained and evidenced.

4
00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:41.390
Continue with Agree responsibilities and acceptance. Then Monitor supplier obligations. Verify the results against the intended outcome.

5
00:00:41.390 --> 00:01:02.120
Stronger evidence looks like this: Stronger: contemporaneous selection scores, signed agreements, supplier performance reviews tied to real work. Weaker evidence would be: Weaker: assuming a signed contract guarantees supplier performance; no trace of consistent use. Triangulate independent sources.

6
00:01:02.120 --> 00:01:16.370
Now your turn. Review four documents and two interviews, identify inconsistencies and complete the mastery challenge. This video is an independent teaching explanation, not official CMMI model wording.
